  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a fourteen-song set on Friday, October 28, 2005, at the Fuel Rocket Club on the Dartmouth College campus in Hanover, New Hampshire [1][2]. This concert is the eighty-ninth of four hundred and sixty-seven archived shows for the band on the Internet Archive [2]. The recording, titled tmg2005-10-28, was taped by Peter Sohriakoff and runs for fifty-nine minutes [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as Source Decay, Southwood Plantation Road, Tallahassee, Cotton, Love Love Love, Dance Music, Jenny, Game Shows Touch Our Lives, Dinu Lipatti's Bones, Lion's Teeth, Baboon, Pet Politics, Against Pollution, and See America Right [1]. The song Pet Politics is noted as rare, with only six archived performances in the collection [1]. The uploader’s description indicates that the performance included an encore featuring the Prayers & Tears of Arthur Digby Sellers [1]. This is the only available recording of the event, making it the recommended source for listeners [1]. The previous archived show for the band took place on October 27, 2005, at Remis Auditorium in the Museum of Fine Arts [2]. The recording provides a complete capture of the evening's musical lineup, documenting the specific order of songs played during the set [1]. Listeners can expect a full hour of music from this specific date and venue, preserving the live atmosphere of the performance [1][2].",
